  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "dd5ea7672120b7f5c6bc5adb03be7e7cce35b542",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 681506612,
          "type": null,
          "body": "So why are the Homebrew paths so different between 64-bit x86 and 64-bit ARM, i.e. the former is /usr/local and the latter is /opt/homebrew?\n\nAnd when looking for what I presume are the Homebrew versions of GNU gettext and Qt, it looks in /usr/local/opt on x86 and /opt/homebrew/opt on Arm?  Is that second \"opt\" redundant?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-20T00:01:34.937Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-20T00:01:34.937Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 117462608,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4242,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "394222dccf74cb46d0b98d3e23c1703207c0083d",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 681507298,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Here's kinda the summery as I understand it...\n\nHomebrew took after ports, and claimed `/usr/local` - on Intel it complains incessantly if you install packages from any other source\n\nWith ASi they moved to a more sensible place, under `/opt` (remember there are limited places where data can be stored in modern macOS due to read only root filesystems)\n\nSo they decide its the right thing to move the entire Homebrew system under what would have been a better place in the beginning, `/opt/homebrew` because its an optional, vendor defined tree.\n\nNow Homebrew basically re-implements the filesystem hierarchy standard at its root, with `bin`, `lib`, `share` etc\n\nMeaning that the full path for the install of `qt5` is actually - funny enough `/opt/homebrew/opt/qt5` with bin, lib etc under that tree.\n\nIt would be possible to just include `/opt/homebrew/lib` as a library, but it may link qt to whatever qt current is...",
          "author": {
            "id": 9765948,
            "username": "rickmark1",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Rick Mark",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/03e5a00720fe630053752df1fb44d033da122794c1e3aa4d130a0bacb83f4f52?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rickmark1"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-20T00:06:55.957Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-20T00:06:55.957Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 117462608,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4242,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "7f05c90efac28ee32912e34defee10b574832543",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 681509516,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> With ASi they moved to a more sensible place, under `/opt` (remember there are limited places where data can be stored in modern macOS due to read only root filesystems)\n\nThen it might be more future-proof to treat x86-64 as the oddball, and set it to /opt/homebrew everywhere except x86-64.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-20T00:22:07.270Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-20T00:22:07.270Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 117462608,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4242,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fdd6427c89ee7af87730ee5e080f9799c1fd1cdf",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 681511563,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Sensible\n\nI also got feedback the best way to handle this is to first:\n\n`which brew` to test if homebrew is on the path at all (probably error and fail build if its not and IS APPLE)\nthat will give a fully qualified path to `brew`\n\nthen execute `brew --prefix` to get the path.  \n\nThis makes no decisions based on architecture at all, but instead directly depends on PATH and `brew` being the arbiter\n\nOn top of this everything that builds on Mac has this same problem, might be most sensible to also create a standard cmake module so these things are handled automatically when platform is APPLE\n\nWill re-work that commit to the above plan which is even more future proof (but perhaps not as back-compatible).  I think its sensible to say that an up-to-date brew install which has `--prefix` is a simple requirement (older macOS builders might need to update their brew install)",
          "author": {
            "id": 9765948,
            "username": "rickmark1",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Rick Mark",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/03e5a00720fe630053752df1fb44d033da122794c1e3aa4d130a0bacb83f4f52?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rickmark1"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-20T00:43:43.305Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-20T00:43:43.305Z",
