        {
          "id": 682493306,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I think in this case `brew --prefix` will work fine, as you can use PATH to create a relationship to the brew install with if `/usr/local/bin` or `/opt/homebrew/bin` is at a higher precedence no?  Brew, being Ruby and not Mach-O binaries works fine at either path (as long as it finds \"a ruby\" which runs the script)\n\nI assume the plan still includes building native-on-native and no Universal2 binary... So why is x-compilation a concern?",
