    {
      "id": "75429e4921de43e68af6d1c592d5f9ec23b31abe",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 682505072,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> Because on earlier versions of homebrew on Intel, homebrew paths are the standard local paths. That's why it was moved, is so it would stop \"taking over\" `/usr/local` you still have libs in `/usr/local/lib` in your case which is where homebrew on Intel would have linked them...\n\nSo will this change cause builds not to work on my machine?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-20T21:53:25.895Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-20T21:56:36.584Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 117462608,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4242,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 682506303,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I don't believe so, but mind verifying?\n\nWe do not remove `/usr/local/lib` from the library path, only add `/usr/local/opt/qt5/lib` in the case of Qt etc, as long as there are valid dyLibs there it should be a standard search path...",
          "author": {
            "id": 9765948,
            "username": "rickmark1",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Rick Mark",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/03e5a00720fe630053752df1fb44d033da122794c1e3aa4d130a0bacb83f4f52?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rickmark1"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-20T21:56:36.549Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-20T21:56:36.549Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 117462608,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4242,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 682682735,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "OK, it seems to work on my Homebrewless system.\n\nBut, again, this isn't \"fixing the ARM64 build on macOS\", it's \"fixing the ARM64 build on macOS *for Homebrew users*\", so the commit message should indicate that; either 1) the build already works for, and on, ARM64 for people not using Homebrew, in which case there's nothing to fix or 2) it doesn't work for those people, in which case this doesn't fix the complete problem.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
