    {
      "id": "b4004e5f22ccd71f9eecf0b09b6a985a8e1645a4",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 683618788,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> I think this should all be handled in a new `cmake/HomebrewPlugin.cmake` file that gets contributed to upstream.\n\n\"Upstream\" as in cmake.org?\n\n> Open question: should this error if not on Apple or if homebrew is not found?\n\nAs long as it can be used in a CMake build process that will, itself, not fail if not on an Apple platform and not fail if on an Apple platform that lacks Homebrew - just as, for example, CMake build processes can be set up that use pkg-config if available but *not* require it.",
